OL,3,GNEWSAFrom jumpers to slug pellets - how
OL,4,ABritish wool is back in demand
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe price of wool has increased more
OL,7,Fthan 70% in the last year, helped in
OL,8,Fpart by a smaller British flock of
OL,9,Fsheep and a dwindling of the global
OL,10,Fstockpile produced during the Covid-19
OL,11,Fpandemic.
OL,13,FPrices reached a 10-year high earlier
OL,14,Fthis year, and comes after some farmers
OL,15,Fburnt fleeces in protest against how
OL,16,Flittle they were being paid.
OL,18,FOn average, a kilogram of clean shorn
OL,19,Fwool sold for #2.54 in the most recent
OL,20,Fsale, compared with less than #1.50 a
OL,21,Fyear ago.
OL,23,APub: 18-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,440,430,260,140,0,100
